- Project implements a Shadow Calendar Sync system that creates "busy" blocks on work calendars based on personal calendar events
- Core components:
  - OAuth Authentication (Google Calendar)
  - Webhook Listener for real-time updates
  - Polling Sync Service (fallback)
  - Sync Engine (core logic)
  - User Settings Management
  - Audit Logging

- Kubernetes deployment strategy:
  - API Server → Kubernetes Deployment
  - Webhook Listener → Kubernetes Deployment
  - Polling Sync Service → Kubernetes CronJob
  - Worker Pods → Kubernetes Deployment with Queue
  - Database → Kubernetes StatefulSet
  - Monitoring → Prometheus & Grafana

- Privacy-first design:
  - No personal event details stored
  - OAuth tokens encrypted at rest
  - Minimal data retention

- Follow sync patterns from technical-notes.md for event handling
 
